---
description: Fuse security and public-demo rules
globs: apps/**,infra/**
alwaysApply: true
---

The public demo may run only allowlisted synthetic scenarios and tools. Never
accept arbitrary code, arbitrary URLs, arbitrary tool definitions, or unbounded
prompts. Do not expose AWS credentials or secrets in frontend code. Validate all
input on the server with Zod. Use least-privilege IAM. Apply run duration, step,
concurrency, and rate limits.

If Bedrock is unavailable, show an honest failure and offer simulation mode. Never
present a pre-recorded run as a live Bedrock run.
